  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Dynetics obligated $1B in FY2026 to date across 47 awards, with an average award size of $22.1M. Dynetics obligations were up 63.3% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, accounting for $1B in obligations. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration and the General Services Administration are smaller buyers at $8.4M and $2.5M respectively. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest market for Dynetics at $870M, followed by Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $133M. Additional markets reporting obligations include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $12.8M and Engineering Services at $10.8M. The FY21 through FY26 series shows year-by-year obligations of $420M, $178M, $117M, $137M, $636M, and $1B. These figures reflect fiscal-year-to-date obligations and the dataset notes that current-year totals are partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Dynetics' top federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1B to Dynetics in FY2026 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $8.4M and the General Services Administration obligated $2.5M. These three agencies are the leading buyers by obligation value in the current fiscal period."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets account for Dynetics' obligations?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest market for Dynetics at $870M. Other Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing accounts for $133M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) accounts for $12.8M, and Engineering Services accounts for $10.8M."
      }
    ]
